Chat backend (./chatbackend on the server, not in this repo): rate limits
that work behind Caddy, and a cap on new conversations.

- index.js: app.set('trust proxy', 1). The server sits behind Caddy, so
  without it every request had Caddy's address and all users shared one
  express-rate-limit allowance (2000 per 15 min): a busy hour, or one
  abuser, locked everyone out of chat.
- dm_routes.js: one account may start at most 30 new conversations an
  hour (opening an existing one doesn't count) — 429 TOO_MANY_NEW_CHATS.

(Message size — 8000 characters — empty messages, and the per-socket
send/typing rate were already limited in dm_socket.js.)

Applied on the server 2026-10-31 (backup:
~/backups/chatbackend-src-20261031-pre-ratelimits.tgz).
  cd ~/treepnet/chatbackend && patch -p1 < chat-rate-limits.patch
  cd .. && docker compose build chatbackend && docker compose up -d chatbackend

